    {
      "id": "R8176-1",
      "type": "PROOF_OBLIGATION",
      "priority": 2,
      "location": "note Premises and declared objects, family value and Why this is the right quantity",
      "finding": "The universal ratio definition excludes A=0 trees. An isolated seed has only its singleton tree: E=A=F=0,S=1, so the budget holds for every c but the stated ratio minimum has empty domain. Hence c>=c* iff coverage over all realizations is not established as written.",
      "repair": "Define the feasible-budget threshold directly including A=0 (and state c domain), or restrict ratio claims to realizations where it applies and prove only the ZA lower bound for uniform budgets. Do not replace ratio by a clamped number silently; W3 negative ratio remains a witness statistic."
    },
    {
      "id": "R8176-2",
      "type": "OVERCLAIM",
      "priority": 2,
      "location": "note Result up front, T4.1, Prior art, Boundaries; campaign appends",
      "finding": "Four exact super-solutions certify four supplied-recursion points, not an optimal p=453 bound, all p>=453 region, or an ordered-phase theorem. Tree coverage is only one needed input; stochastic domination/count and physical application are neither re-proved here nor supplied by unlanded8174/8175. Located strength p\u224811 and factor35 inherit a historical simulation claim explicitly narrowed on current main8172. Original8175 does not prove global construction sharpness2, repeated here.",
      "repair": "Retain four point certificates and necessary scalar exclusion under explicit supplied recurrence/budget conditions. Remove best-ever/true-strength/global2 claims and physical phase inference; cite corrected main8172 as context only if needed. Preserve deferred upstream science rather than importing authority."
    },
    {
      "id": "R8176-3",
      "type": "NO_GO_OVERCLAIM",
      "priority": 2,
      "location": "note T4.2, headline, claim_scope and lower-than368 sentences",
      "finding": "Crossing between integer367 and368 proves integer exclusion p<=367. For real positive p the root is (725+sqrt557525)/4; the stated calculation does not exclude all real p<368. Exact p=36799/100 has d3<4/729.",
      "repair": "Specify integer p for rounded floor, or state the exact scalar necessary inequality 4p^2-1450p-7975>0. The test p367.99 is not itself a complete recurrence certificate."
    },
    {
      "id": "R8176-4",
